.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge update'\/\fR
[1;34musage: [0m[1;35msysforge update[0m [[32m\-h[0m] [[36m\-\-dry\-run[0m] [[36m\-\-devel[0m] [[36m\-\-offline[0m] [[36m\-\-install\-only[0m] [[36m\-\-packages [33mFILE[0m] [[36m\-\-state\-dir [33mDIR[0m]
                       [[36m\-\-profile\-conf [33mFILE[0m] [[36m\-\-cache\-report[0m] [[36m\-\-no\-pkg\-log[0m] [[36m\-\-persist\-log[0m] [[36m\-\-log\-dir [33mDIR[0m]
                       [[36m\-\-makepkg [33mFLAGS[0m] [[36m\-\-interactive[0m] [[36m\-\-no\-cleanbuild[0m] [[36m\-\-cleansrc[0m]
                       [32m[PKG ...][0m

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
Limit update to these package names (default: all sysforge\-managed packages).

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge update'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be rebuilt without doing it.

.TP
\fB\-\-devel\fR
Resolve and rebuild VCS packages (\-git, \-svn, \-hg, \-bzr) whose upstream HEAD has advanced past the installed
version. Resolution runs makepkg \-\-nobuild per VCS package; up\-to\-date packages are skipped, not rebuilt. Per\-
package upstream commits recorded in build_state are reused on subsequent runs to short\-circuit the resolve via git
ls\-remote.

.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
No network: skip git pulls, clones, and AUR RPC. Pure local version check.

.TP
\fB\-\-install\-only\fR
Skip rebuild; install only those locally\-built artifacts in PKGDEST that are newer than the installed version.
Implies \-\-offline. Mutually exclusive with \-\-makepkg, \-\-no\-cleanbuild, \-\-cleansrc, \-\-interactive, and \-\-cache\-
report.

.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml for override rules (default: /home/keith/src/sysforge/tests/data/etc/sysforge/packages.toml).

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the run.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR
Disable per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR
Extra flags passed verbatim to makepkg (e.g. \-m '\-f' to force rebuild). Combined short flags are expanded: \-sfci
becomes \-s \-f \-c \-i.

.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
Pause on build failures to allow manual correction (default: log failure and continue).

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cleanbuild\fR
Skip the automatic \-\-cleanbuild (\-C) added for update runs. Useful when packages are already built and you only need
to re\-run the install step.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
Purge each package's src dir and re\-clone before building. Per\-package fatal if the clone has uncommitted changes,
unpushed commits, or no upstream — that package is reported failed and the run continues.

