.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge doctor'\/\fR
[1;34musage: [0m[1;35msysforge doctor[0m [[32m\-h[0m] [[36m\-\-graphics[0m] [[36m\-\-all[0m] [[36m\-\-repo[0m] [[36m\-\-shallow[0m] [[36m\-\-quiet[0m] [[36m\-\-suggest[0m] [32m[PKG ...][0m

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
One or more installed package names to verify. Without any PKG/\-\-graphics/\-\-all, the command exits with usage.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge doctor'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-graphics\fR
Expand to the graphics stack (mesa, vulkan, libglvnd, wayland, libdrm, libva, libvdpau, egl\-wayland, xwayland,
gamescope, plus per\-vendor drivers from the hardware overlay's gpu_vendors) AND run system\-state probes (nvidia\-drm
modeset, driver version skew, Wayland explicit\-sync protocol, Steam GPU accel, session type).

.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Verify every installed package — foreign and non\-foreign (pacman \-Q). Slow but comprehensive.

.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR
Verify every non\-foreign (native repo) package. Narrower than \-\-all.

.TP
\fB\-\-shallow\fR
Do not recurse into transitive dependencies of each target.

.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR, \fB\-q\fR
Suppress clean lines; print only packages with issues.

.TP
\fB\-\-suggest\fR, \fB\-s\fR
For each unsatisfied soname, look up candidate packages via `pacman \-Fq`. Findings split into 'install candidates'
(missing from disk — install the package) and 'ABI\-drift candidates' (present but one of their versioned symbols no
longer resolves — rebuild or upgrade, not reinstall). Requires a synced files db (`sudo pacman \-Fy`).

